module Core

### The protocol for values that can produce an independent DEEP copy of themselves — a new object
### with its own lifetime, sharing no externally visible mutable state. `Copyable` and `Storable` are
### ORTHOGONAL capabilities, NOT a hierarchy: a value record obeys both; an RC handle is `Storable`
### (share) but not `Copyable` (a shared handle's referent cannot be deep-duplicated); an `entity` is
### `Copyable` (heap deep-clone) but not `Storable` (single-owner, moved via `steal`, never implicitly
### bound). `copy` is inserted wherever an independent duplicate is required — at assignment and at
### every materialization point (e.g. building a value into a collection).
protocol Copyable
needs Copyable everywhere
  ### Returns a deep, independent copy of this value.
  ### :returns: A copy of this value with its own valid lifetime and invariants.
  @readonly
  routine Me.copy() -> Me
